{"author":{"id":"f21006d1826991d76b358f177209294474e8c2701fc659ff8fe8b8f40ee77f55"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1677963759,"nonce":"6w+MKogKf9pXALQh7ae/q6XvyUE=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh85Wt5-q","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/327#issuecomment-1454874538"},"message":"Maybe I'm misunderstanding something, but why wouldn't we be able to call out to whatever is configured with [`credential.helper`](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitcredentials#Documentation/gitcredentials.txt-helper)?\n\n```\n$ cat /some/git/config\n[credential \"foo\"]\n    helper = !/usr/bin/password-manager --flag1 --flag2 blahblahblah\"\n```\n\nI suppose this has the downside of supporting arbtirary executables, but fetching this information is available via `go-git` , and executing it (grabbing the output) is available via [`os/exec`](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec) and friends.\n\nAssuming the configured helper is secure, this leaves `git-bug` with the same responsibility it would have if using some other backend; that is, ensuring that the received contents are secure and ideally zeroed-out or otherwise removed from memory after usage ([`memguard`](https://github.com/awnumar/memguard)?).","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1677963804,"nonce":"uZkpWOAEb0cIxLWCN5zmd10aFu0=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALOCGKeh85Wt5-qzi4bzKE"},"target":"615b8f9334c6f36002f2aeed94d9dee3d02ed7e0283dfc1106c18ba662341725","message":"Maybe I'm misunderstanding something, but why wouldn't we be able to call out to whatever is configured with [`credential.helper`](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitcredentials#Documentation/gitcredentials.txt-helper)?\n\n```\n$ cat /some/git/config\n[credential \"foo\"]\n    helper = \"/usr/bin/password-manager --flag1 --flag2 blahblahblah\"\n```\n\nI suppose this has the downside of supporting arbtirary executables, but fetching this information is available via `go-git` , and executing it (grabbing the output) is available via [`os/exec`](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec) and friends.\n\nAssuming the configured helper is secure, this leaves `git-bug` with the same responsibility it would have if using some other backend; that is, ensuring that the received contents are secure and ideally zeroed-out or otherwise removed from memory after usage ([`memguard`](https://github.com/awnumar/memguard)?).","files":null}]}